# DTF tier manifest: curation-popularity-download-checks  (artifact-keeper#5274, PR #5275 / 1.12.0)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single, plus the mock npm upstream and the
# json-file log driver for the backend (the oracle greps its flag line).
#
# #5274 lets a `popularity` curation rule run its name checks (typo-squat,
# homoglyph/mixed-script, affix) on npm and PyPI Remote and Virtual
# downloads, but only when the rule opts in with
# `"download_name_checks": true`. Without the key a rule behaves exactly as
# before: it runs only in the staging sync, and downloads are unchanged.
#
# Topology: the mock npm upstream (upstreams.mock-npm) serves one package,
# `dtf-held` 1.0.0, under any path prefix. Every rule uses a custom popular
# list `["dtf-hold"]`, so:
#   * `dtf-held` is one edit from `dtf-hold`: an edit-distance match, which
#     only ever FLAGS on a download (served, flag line logged).
#   * `dtf-hоld` (Cyrillic о, U+043E) is a homoglyph of `dtf-hold`: with
#     `block_typosquat: true` it is refused with 403 curation_blocked before
#     any upstream request.
#
# Repositories (all npm, curation default action `allow`):
#   ON    Remote, curation on, opted-in rule {download_name_checks, block_typosquat}
#   VON   Virtual over NONE, curation on, the same opted-in rule on the Virtual
#         (npm applies the Virtual's own rules)
#   OFF   Remote, curation on, the same rule WITHOUT download_name_checks
#         (a rule as written before #5274)
#   NONE  Remote, curation off, no rules
#   PYON  PyPI Remote, curation on, opted-in rule with popular list ["click"]
#   PYOFF PyPI Remote, curation on, the same rule WITHOUT download_name_checks
#
# Cases:
#   FIX #5274   ON refuses the homoglyph tarball: 403 curation_blocked, and
#               the mock saw no request for it.
#   FIX #5274   ON serves `dtf-held` and the backend logs the flag line
#               naming the package.
#   FIX #5274   VON refuses the homoglyph tarball: 403 curation_blocked.
#   FIX #5274   creating the OFF rule on a Remote returns a `warnings` entry
#               naming download_name_checks; the opted-in rule returns none.
#   CONTROL     OFF serves `dtf-held`, does not 403 the homoglyph, and logs no
#               flag line for OFF (upgrade safety: an existing rule changes
#               no download).
#   FIX #5274   PYON refuses the ASCII confusable `c1ick` (simple index,
#               403 curation_blocked). PyPI refuses non-PEP 508 names, so an
#               ASCII confusable is the only lookalike that reaches the check.
#   CONTROL     PYOFF does not refuse `c1ick`.
#   CONTROL     NONE serves `dtf-held` and does not 403 the homoglyph.
#
# Red on an image without #5275 (ghcr ...:main before the merge): every FIX
# case fails (no name checks on downloads, no warnings field); every CONTROL
# passes. Green on the #5275 image.
COVERS="5274"
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-npm logging.json-file"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
